      "writtenOn": "2017-01-27T07:23:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let\u0027s document the need for this check. Without reading the commit message it seemed out of place\n\n// Issue https://golang.org/issues/17060. We should check that the plaintextKey\n// length is equal to the cipherFunc keysize to account for AES192.\nif keyLen, keySize :\u003d len(plaintextKey), cipherFunc.KeySize(); keyLen !\u003d keySize {\n    return nil, cipherFunc, errors.StructuralError(fmt.Sprintf(\"incorrect key size %d expected %d\", keySize, keyLen))\n}\n\nAlso the past checks seemed to work for the other ciphers, is there a reason why we should entirely remove\nthe condition:\nl \u003d\u003d 0 || l %cipherFunc.blockSize() !\u003d 0 {",
      "revId": "ee6cc3eda223ba0d0c91a2a8d65b31e59a38b888",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": true
    },
